        "release_date": "1980-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "description": "1. Prepare for lab safety incidents: Put on safety equipment before your experiment. Wear safety glasses and a lab coat.\n2. How to operate an alkaline lamp: Find the alkaline lamp and igniter, place it on the white table, and flick the flame to experience fire.\n3. burn treatment: soak the burned area in water to reduce the heat and wrap it with clean gauze.\n4. Staunching wounds: Use clean gauze to staunch bleeding if a tool breaks during the experiment.\n5. organize experimental tools: put the alcohol lamp in the display case after the experiment is finished.\n6. fire response: If a fire occurs, use the fire extinguisher near the door to extinguish the fire.",
